 "notes": [
  "measured: a real federation. simulated: numpy, with clip, grid and noise variance read from a plan the system signed for that many sites. The simulation rounds a Gaussian where the system draws an exact discrete one.",
  "A canary that is absent still joins and adds noise; only its update is empty. That matches the guarantee, which is about what a site contributed.",
  "The bound is a lower bound. With m canaries it cannot exceed about log of m over the error budget, so a small real run can only show a small one.",
  "membership_accuracy is site-level membership inference on the same scores, with the threshold at half the clip; 0.5 is chance.",
  "The control with the noise left out gives the ceiling of the audit at that many canaries. Where the ceiling is below the claim, the audit could not have contradicted the claim, and passing it says little.",
  "Membership inference on individuals inside a site was not run. The guarantee is per site."
 ]
